Fix the line count shown by ".import" on 32-bit big-endian platforms

The number of lines of input in the summary printed by ".import" is
computed as "sCtx.nLine-1-iLineOffset".  Because iLineOffset is an i64
this is a 64-bit value, but it was formatted with %d, which reads a
32-bit int.  On 32-bit big-endian platforms (s390) the high word of the
64-bit value is read, which is always 0, so test/import01.sql fails
there.  Use %lld.

--- a/src/shell.c.in
+++ b/src/shell.c.in
@@ -8731,7 +8731,7 @@
   if( needCommit ) sqlite3_exec(p->db, "COMMIT", 0, 0, 0);
   if( eVerbose>0 ){
     cli_printf(p->out,
-          "Added %d rows with %d errors using %d lines of input\n",
+          "Added %d rows with %d errors using %lld lines of input\n",
           sCtx.nRow, sCtx.nErr, sCtx.nLine-1-iLineOffset);
   }
   return sCtx.nErr ? 1 : 0;
